insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('37a39f47-ed41-5d5e-90c1-0134d9bbdc08', 'da566530-f509-5133-b265-9183e82e99e2', 'Today or yesterday: the stress tells', '**Hoy laburo**, **ayer laburé**. The same verb, and only the stress moves: *LA-bu-ro* is now, *la-bu-RÉ* is done. Say it out loud and the past is already right.', 'draft'),
  ('575cb41d-92ef-5b02-b25e-72e5a15b2ea0', 'da566530-f509-5133-b265-9183e82e99e2', 'Fui: two verbs, one word', '**Fui** is both *I went* (ir) and *I was* (ser). **Fui a la cancha** — *I went to the game*; **fue re lindo** — *it was really nice*. The sentence always tells you which.', 'draft'),
  ('4cd37e48-1a86-5910-948e-66deaab58202', 'ca8f891d-0d08-51d6-84de-10ce90c0245f', 'The irregular ones have no accent', '**Hice, vi, dije, pude, vine** — the pasts you use most carry no accent, unlike *laburé* or *comí*. **¿Qué hiciste?** — **Nada, vi una peli.**', 'draft'),
  ('f14e675f-3b81-58ce-92bd-dc0406370194', 'ca8f891d-0d08-51d6-84de-10ce90c0245f', 'Better and worse', '**Mejor** and **peor** never take *más*: **está mejor**, **fue peor**. And *-ísimo* is the porteño way to say *really*: **riquísimo**, **carísimo**.', 'draft'),
  ('8002b7a0-5ac8-590a-9a69-977951aa25e0', '8531d298-54ee-59f6-9973-5e4562177f2e', 'The little word goes on the end', 'In a request the pronoun sticks to the verb: **llamame**, **mandame**, **dame**, **prestame**. In a statement it goes in front: **te llamo**, **me mandás**.', 'draft'),
  ('95be973e-2407-5c68-bc34-cf9e112dc823', '8531d298-54ee-59f6-9973-5e4562177f2e', 'Whose turn is it?', '**Me toca lavar** — *it''s my turn to wash up*. **¿A quién le toca?** Porteños split the chores with *tocar*, never with *turno*.', 'draft'),
  ('d14d3ee0-aa95-5ffd-ab43-f1d7d87dfc74', 'a0a421e1-d5be-5c04-a905-e4bd5424aa57', 'The scene and the event', '**Era**, **tenía**, **estaba** paint the scene — how things were. **Fui**, **tuve**, **llegó** are what happened in it. **Estaba lloviendo cuando llegó Juan.**', 'draft'),
  ('267eddc7-6907-5ed5-a521-c9d81fdc0120', 'a0a421e1-d5be-5c04-a905-e4bd5424aa57', 'Used to', 'English says *used to*; Spanish just uses the imperfect. **Jugábamos en la calle** — *we used to play in the street*. **Siempre**, **a veces** and **de chico** go with it.', 'draft'),
  ('54958d4f-50e8-5d54-a404-928792675702', 'b38bd9a1-f0a8-5fe1-9aa1-0e8260930af6', 'Pido, pedí, pidió', '**Pedir** changes its vowel: **pido** today, **pedí** yesterday, and **pidió** for someone else. **¿Qué pediste?** — **Pedí un bife.**', 'draft'),
  ('ed6072dc-6128-51a8-83b7-26e45cf6ccde', 'b38bd9a1-f0a8-5fe1-9aa1-0e8260930af6', 'Tipo ocho', '**Tipo** makes a time loose: **tipo ocho** is *around eight*, and in Buenos Aires that means eight-thirty. For exactly eight, say **a las ocho en punto**.', 'draft'),
  ('459ce15a-8a6b-5cd0-a8cb-d2f762e68335', '2a6a2955-3702-5c32-a348-a1d2c591bdf2', 'Me puse: it happened to you', '**Me puse nervioso**, **me enojé**, **me asusté** — a feeling that came over you at one moment is the preterite. **Estaba nervioso** is the state you were in.', 'draft'),
  ('3e33b8ba-1526-5cde-95a7-43b8b9afcc60', '2a6a2955-3702-5c32-a348-a1d2c591bdf2', 'Plans with voy a', 'For plans, porteños use **voy a** + verb far more than the future: **la semana que viene voy a descansar**. **Pienso** and **tengo ganas de** do the same job.', 'draft'),
  ('9f58a4a6-f33d-5dc6-b948-90e3bffe9d0f', '6cbcbdaf-a420-507d-844b-34d87b2822f2', 'Asking nicely', '**¿Me pasás la sal?** is how you ask at the table — a question in the present. **¿Podrías…?** is softer, for a bigger favor.', 'draft'),
  ('ac292dce-4ca4-5745-b720-c39233bc02eb', '6cbcbdaf-a420-507d-844b-34d87b2822f2', 'Hay que, tenés que, no hace falta', '**Hay que** is *it has to be done* — nobody in particular. **Tenés que** is *you have to*. **No hace falta** is *there''s no need*.', 'draft'),
  ('c69d6cff-ff9d-5cb7-84a1-e7f685916f4c', '05dc3d96-dc93-54a8-9eec-ca5cc9baff16', 'Me quedé sin…', '**Me quedé sin batería**, **sin plata**, **sin laburo** — *I ran out of*. It is the preterite: it happened at one moment.', 'draft'),
  ('c975280b-817a-5375-b749-0900db51bc69', '05dc3d96-dc93-54a8-9eec-ca5cc9baff16', 'Give it back', '**Devolveme las llaves**, **dejame pasar**, **traeme el cargador** — in requests the pronoun rides on the end, and it''s always *me*.', 'draft'),
  ('44389a51-83e3-518b-b2cf-b6316386706d', '1c4eaeb1-2bcc-5b49-889e-bfd0ac2ed088', 'Guessing with the future', '**¿Dónde estará?** is not about tomorrow: it is *I wonder where he is*. The future guesses; **capaz** and **seguro que** do it in the present.', 'draft'),
  ('049084f0-7771-58c3-81c6-13f81ad731a0', '1c4eaeb1-2bcc-5b49-889e-bfd0ac2ed088', 'Me siento, lo siento', '**Me siento mal** — *I feel bad*. **Lo siento** — *I''m sorry*, for real bad news. For bumping into someone, say **perdón**.', 'draft'),
  ('07ebc383-a188-5ff3-9918-2cd9e97019d1', 'ef00ab7c-09e9-5c6b-8389-aa83a371e3d1', 'Wanting someone else to', '**Quiero ir** — *I want to go*. **Quiero que vayas** — *I want you to go*. When the wish is about someone else, the second verb turns subjunctive.', 'draft'),
  ('4470f843-1dae-5511-b927-174a9bf0cbb1', 'ef00ab7c-09e9-5c6b-8389-aa83a371e3d1', 'Cuando about the future', '**Cuando llegás, me avisás** is a habit; **cuando llegues, avisame** is one future time. For what hasn''t happened yet, *cuando* takes the subjunctive.', 'draft'),
  ('23237cc6-4f06-5436-98d4-0d6ad6ff71b9', 'a46178fb-2c93-503a-b057-1838974c2a73', 'Creo que / no creo que', '**Creo que viene** — the indicative, because you believe it. **No creo que venga** — the subjunctive, because you doubt it.', 'draft'),
  ('80340f0f-566d-5ec8-b4c2-167d8998c48a', 'a46178fb-2c93-503a-b057-1838974c2a73', 'Don''t!', 'A negative command is the subjunctive: **no te preocupes**, **no te olvides**, **no digas nada**. **Probá** becomes **no pruebes**.', 'draft'),
  ('0d02fdcf-fd59-57f9-b09c-94119f2c9f2e', 'a53cea7e-02aa-56f7-a3b8-de1dca112674', 'Qué bueno que…', 'A reaction to someone else''s news takes the subjunctive: **qué bueno que estés acá**, **me alegro que te vaya bien**, **qué lástima que no puedas venir**.', 'draft'),
  ('19ab87a1-4728-5574-85c7-d46315fe8316', 'a53cea7e-02aa-56f7-a3b8-de1dca112674', 'Sé, sabés, ni idea', '**Sé** (with an accent) is *I know*. **¿Sabés?** — *do you know?* And the porteño *I have no idea*: **ni idea**.', 'draft'),
  ('f4ed9ba7-049b-5b3f-a8ac-c10dade176d9', 'ce05c318-270e-5388-9073-3793ff249013', 'If I had, I would', '**Si tuviera plata, viajaría.** The *if* half takes *tuviera, fuera, pudiera*; the other half takes *-ía*: *iría, haría, sería*.', 'draft'),
  ('ade978ac-cf4e-5fde-a04b-a5c2f59f8651', 'ce05c318-270e-5388-9073-3793ff249013', 'Yo que vos', 'Porteño advice starts with **yo que vos** — *if I were you* — and goes straight to the conditional: **yo que vos, no le diría nada**.', 'draft'),
  ('21df4945-5b04-5807-bdcc-3103bdd9ae06', 'a895f900-29bb-56a3-8161-0d08826cfe48', 'No me alcanza', '**No me alcanza** — *it''s not enough (for me)*. It works for money, time, anything: **no me alcanza la plata**, **no me alcanza el tiempo**.', 'draft'),
  ('d39dad46-046e-5481-a0ab-6c5e8eb7b09d', 'a895f900-29bb-56a3-8161-0d08826cfe48', 'Dicen que, parece que', 'Pass on news without owning it: **dicen que va a llover** — *they say it''s going to rain*; **parece que Juan se mudó** — *looks like Juan moved*.', 'draft'),
  ('4c1db3a5-2550-504b-b553-a7c7655b08aa', '3e9f1f79-1601-518d-ad4c-5540cd98f35b', 'Queda for places', '**¿Dónde queda?** — *where is it?* for a place on the map. **Me queda cerca** — *it''s close to me*. People **están**; places **quedan**.', 'draft'),
  ('31218369-6463-5d5f-91ce-abbcb550021c', '3e9f1f79-1601-518d-ad4c-5540cd98f35b', 'He said he was coming', 'Report what someone said and the tense steps back: **viene** becomes **dijo que venía**.', 'draft'),
  ('2f6a0df7-0524-5701-bbaa-7b930c8ea956', 'a64eb13a-e442-5199-bf7e-cbdf6e56de26', 'It fell on me', '**Se me cayó el vaso** — the glass fell, and it happened to me. No blame: that is why every porteño story of a mishap starts with **se me**.', 'draft'),
  ('e7ad6bd5-1193-5f72-a8d8-63952ab02e51', 'a64eb13a-e442-5199-bf7e-cbdf6e56de26', 'Ya había', '**Ya había comido** — *I had already eaten* — puts one past before another: **cuando llegaste, ya había comido**.', 'draft'),
  ('c458a9ac-cd4c-5a51-833c-9e9f01372152', '080920e1-dfcc-555f-94e8-0864285aa5e7', 'No anda', 'A machine that doesn''t work **no anda**: **no anda el ascensor**, **el wifi no anda**. **Funciona** is correct, but it''s what the manual says.', 'draft'),
  ('fef74f62-1902-548c-8a1f-9530412881f4', '080920e1-dfcc-555f-94e8-0864285aa5e7', 'Depende', '**Depende**, **puede ser**, **en parte** — the porteño hedge. Full agreement is **estoy de acuerdo**; full disagreement, **para nada**.', 'draft'),
  ('01ba9a08-394a-56c1-b92e-0373f545224a', 'f1ba775f-ad41-52d5-ae7c-9ee7834def48', 'Me dio miedo', '**Me da miedo** is *it scares me* in general; **me dio miedo** is one scare, over and done. The thing that scares you is the subject: **me dan miedo los perros**.', 'draft'),
  ('5f78e70b-ea4c-52fc-9052-b018341a59d2', 'f1ba775f-ad41-52d5-ae7c-9ee7834def48', 'Se saluda con un beso', '**Acá se saluda con un beso** — *here people greet with a kiss*. **Se** + verb says what everyone does, no subject needed.', 'draft')
